Rules:
- Start with a 2-3 sentence introduction (no heading) that uses the primary keyword in the first
  100 words, then one "## " section per outline heading, in order. Use "### " only below a "## ".
- Do not write an H1 ("# ") - the title is added separately.
- Every statistic, percentage, number of customers or "research shows" statement must cite a
  research note id like [S1]. If no note supports a claim, leave the claim out.
- Short paragraphs and short sentences (aim for a Flesch reading ease of 60+). Explain jargon.
- Work the secondary keywords in naturally; never stuff keywords.
- End with a short conclusion section that gives the reader one clear next step.
